  "dataGaps": [
    {
      "dimension": "anticipation",
      "indicatorId": "government_foresight_capacity",
      "name": "Government foresight capacity",
      "publisher": "none",
      "reason": "No comparable international dataset. OECD and UN work is descriptive, not scored. Envisioning would have to build this.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "anticipation",
      "indicatorId": "basic_research_share",
      "name": "Long-horizon research share",
      "publisher": "OECD MSTI",
      "reason": "Published by OECD for members only. Missing for India, South Africa, Brazil in comparable form.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "agency",
      "indicatorId": "adult_digital_skills",
      "name": "Adult digital skills",
      "publisher": "ITU",
      "reason": "ITU collects this but coverage across these ten countries is broken and the task lists differ by year.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "agency",
      "indicatorId": "perceived_control",
      "name": "Perceived control over life",
      "publisher": "World Values Survey",
      "reason": "WVS wave 7 covers most of these countries but fieldwork years differ by up to six years, and Singapore is thin.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "coordination",
      "indicatorId": "government_effectiveness",
      "name": "Government effectiveness",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. The WGI aggregate the opinions of experts and firms, and in this set the four WGI series correlate with each other between 0.93 and 0.98 while correlating with log GDP per capita at 0.91. That is one perception of national wealth counted in three dimensions. Cross-agency delivery records are the replacement and they are a declared gap. See D23 and A4.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "coordination",
      "indicatorId": "regulatory_quality",
      "name": "Regulatory quality",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. Same measurement as government effectiveness, filed under a different name, correlating with it above 0.93. See D23 and A4.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "coordination",
      "indicatorId": "logistics_performance",
      "name": "Logistics performance",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. The LPI is a survey of international freight forwarders, so it records how a country looks to global logistics firms. A small country with a small port scores low whatever its state can organise, which is artefact A9. Container throughput and border time are observable and stay. See D23.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "coordination",
      "indicatorId": "university_industry_collaboration",
      "name": "University-industry collaboration",
      "publisher": "Global Innovation Index",
      "reason": "GII carries it, but the underlying item is a WEF executive opinion survey whose microdata is not inspectable. Excluded on principle 4.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "coordination",
      "indicatorId": "civil_society_strength",
      "name": "Civil society strength",
      "publisher": "V-Dem",
      "reason": "V-Dem core civil society index is inspectable and would fill this. Not yet wired; it needs its own ingestion adapter.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "coordination",
      "indicatorId": "public_private_collaboration",
      "name": "Public-private collaboration",
      "publisher": "none",
      "reason": "No comparable dataset. PPP investment databases measure infrastructure finance, not collaboration capacity.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "trust",
      "indicatorId": "rule_of_law",
      "name": "Rule of law",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. A WGI perception composite correlating with control of corruption above 0.95 and with log GDP per capita at 0.83. Court throughput and case clearance rates are the observable replacement and are a declared gap. See D23 and A4.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "trust",
      "indicatorId": "control_of_corruption",
      "name": "Control of corruption",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. A WGI perception composite. It measures reputation for corruption, which is not the same thing as corruption, and it tracks income closely. Prosecution and audit records are the observable replacement and are a declared gap. See D23 and A4.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "trust",
      "indicatorId": "homicide_rate",
      "name": "Intentional homicide rate",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Added 2026-08-26 by D23 as the observable replacement for two retired WGI perception composites, and retired 2026-08-27 by D44 when the diagnostic built in D42 measured what it was doing. It raised this dimension's correlation with log GDP per capita by 0.288, from 0.096 to 0.385, the largest single wealth contribution anywhere in the model. It was added to fix wealth contamination and it was the wealth contamination. The dataset is sound and the objection is to what it measures here: homicide is driven heavily by organised crime, a society can be physically safe while trusting very little, and across this country set the variation it carries is mostly income. Behavioural trust measures remain a gap.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "trust",
      "indicatorId": "interpersonal_trust",
      "name": "Generalised interpersonal trust",
      "publisher": "World Values Survey",
      "reason": "The single most important item in this dimension and the one we cannot currently pull. WVS wave 7 microdata needs a licensed download and manual harmonisation.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "trust",
      "indicatorId": "institutional_trust",
      "name": "Trust in public institutions",
      "publisher": "OECD Trust Survey / WVS",
      "reason": "The OECD survey covers members only. Mixing it with WVS items for India and South Africa would break comparability.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "trust",
      "indicatorId": "willingness_to_cooperate_strangers",
      "name": "Cooperation beyond the in-group",
      "publisher": "World Values Survey",
      "reason": "The distinction that makes this dimension worth measuring. Same licensing obstacle as generalised trust.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "learning",
      "indicatorId": "adult_learning_participation",
      "name": "Adult learning participation",
      "publisher": "Eurostat / OECD PIAAC",
      "reason": "The best available measure of continuous learning capacity, and it exists only for European and OECD members.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "learning",
      "indicatorId": "research_citation_impact",
      "name": "Research citation impact",
      "publisher": "OpenAlex",
      "reason": "Computable from OpenAlex, which is open and inspectable. This is the highest-value gap to close next.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "experimentation",
      "indicatorId": "venture_capital_gdp",
      "name": "Venture capital investment",
      "publisher": "OECD / national VC associations",
      "reason": "Still a gap after a direct check on 2026-08-26. The OECD SME and Entrepreneurship Financing scoreboard is the only inspectable aggregate and it carries venture capital for 6 of these 16 countries, in national currency rather than as a share of GDP, latest year 2022. Brazil, India, South Africa and Singapore are all absent, so wiring it would score the rich half of the set and lower coverage for the rest. Commercial databases cover the world and are not inspectable. Read A1 before treating this dimension as measured.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "experimentation",
      "indicatorId": "regulatory_sandbox_activity",
      "name": "Regulatory sandbox activity",
      "publisher": "none",
      "reason": "Countable from primary sources but nobody maintains a comparable register. A realistic candidate for Envisioning to build.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "experimentation",
      "indicatorId": "university_spinouts",
      "name": "University spinouts",
      "publisher": "national TTO associations",
      "reason": "Reported nationally with incompatible definitions of what counts as a spinout.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "experimentation",
      "indicatorId": "business_rd_share",
      "name": "Business share of R&D",
      "publisher": "UNESCO UIS",
      "reason": "UIS publishes this and it is a good candidate for the next ingestion adapter.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "adaptability",
      "indicatorId": "long_term_unemployment_share",
      "name": "Long-term unemployment share",
      "publisher": "ILOSTAT",
      "reason": "Closer to reallocation speed than the headline rate: it asks whether people who lose work find new work. ILOSTAT publishes it; the World Bank API does not carry it.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "adaptability",
      "indicatorId": "export_diversification",
      "name": "Export diversification",
      "publisher": "UNCTAD",
      "reason": "UNCTAD publishes the concentration index and it is computable. Another good candidate for the next adapter.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "adaptability",
      "indicatorId": "disaster_preparedness",
      "name": "Disaster preparedness and recovery",
      "publisher": "INFORM / UNDRR",
      "reason": "INFORM is largely a hazard-exposure index, so using it here would measure geography rather than capability.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "adaptability",
      "indicatorId": "institutional_responsiveness",
      "name": "Institutional responsiveness",
      "publisher": "none",
      "reason": "No dataset exists. Measurable in principle from legislative and regulatory timestamps, which no one has assembled comparably.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "building",
      "indicatorId": "logistics_infrastructure",
      "name": "Logistics infrastructure quality",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. An LPI sub-index, so the same freight-forwarder survey as logistics performance and the same problem. Electricity connection speed stays as the observable infrastructure measure in this dimension. See D23.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "building",
      "indicatorId": "large_project_delivery",
      "name": "Large project delivery",
      "publisher": "none",
      "reason": "The single best measure of execution capability and there is no comparable international dataset. Assembling one is a defensible Envisioning project. Building mixes industrial output with state delivery capacity, and this indicator carries the delivery side: the other six indicators cannot see a national programme that was delivered. Documented deliveries are recorded in data/evidence and never scored, see D20.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "building",
      "indicatorId": "firm_scale_up_rate",
      "name": "Firm scale-up rate",
      "publisher": "OECD DynEmp",
      "reason": "OECD business dynamics work covers members irregularly. Nothing comparable for India, Brazil or South Africa.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "shared_purpose",
      "indicatorId": "voice_and_accountability",
      "name": "Voice and accountability",
      "publisher": "World Bank",
      "reason": "Retired 2026-08-26. Artefact A5: it measures the democratic channel while Shared Purpose asks whether people can see themselves in a common project. Singapore scored 20.9 while being one of the most effective collective actors in the set. Voter turnout, volunteering and civic participation are the observable replacements and all are declared gaps. See D23 and A5.",
      "status": "retired"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "shared_purpose",
      "indicatorId": "national_belonging",
      "name": "Sense of national belonging",
      "publisher": "World Values Survey",
      "reason": "Culturally loaded. High national pride is not the same as capacity for collective action and must not be read as such.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "shared_purpose",
      "indicatorId": "volunteering_rate",
      "name": "Volunteering",
      "publisher": "Gallup World Poll / CAF",
      "reason": "CAF publishes country figures but the underlying Gallup microdata is proprietary, so it fails the inspectability rule.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "shared_purpose",
      "indicatorId": "political_polarization",
      "name": "Political polarisation",
      "publisher": "V-Dem",
      "reason": "V-Dem political polarisation is inspectable and would fill this. Pluralism is the target, so only hostile polarisation should count against a country.",
      "status": "gap"
    },
    {
      "dimension": "shared_purpose",
      "indicatorId": "civic_participation",
      "name": "Civic participation",
      "publisher": "World Values Survey",
      "reason": "Behavioural rather than attitudinal, so it is the item worth prioritising if only one survey measure can be harmonised.",
      "status": "gap"
    }
